<TrustPage title="Corrections and reporting status | CalcsDesk" description="How CalcsDesk will investigate calculation errors and record corrections, including the current availability of its reporting form." breadcrumb="Corrections" eyebrow="Keep the record clear" heading="A correction should explain what changed." intro="A calculator can be wrong because of its rates, assumptions or implementation. A useful correction identifies the affected tool and version, checks the evidence and explains the impact on the result.">
  <div class="trust-callout"><strong>Reporting form not active yet</strong><p>The protected contact and error-reporting form is being prepared. This page does not receive or submit messages, and no reply-time promise is made while that channel is unavailable.</p></div>
  <h2>What to check first.</h2><p>Compare the result with the calculator’s stated scope, tax year, filing status, assumptions and exclusions. The federal beta uses the basic standard deduction and assumes the same wage base for income tax and FICA. It does not model every tax-return item or reproduce W-4 paycheck withholding.</p><p>You can inspect its <a href="/us/tax/income-tax-calculator/#rates-sources">rate table and official sources</a>, along with the bracket-by-bracket working. An unexplained difference should still be investigated; the scope note is not evidence that an implementation is correct.</p>
  <h2>What will help an investigation.</h2><p>Once the reporting form is available, a useful report will include:</p><ul><li>The page URL and the tax year shown.</li><li>The steps needed to reproduce the issue, using example figures rather than personal records.</li><li>The result you expected and the result shown.</li><li>A link to the official publication or worked example supporting the expected result.</li><li>Whether the issue concerns a rate, a calculation, an explanation or the interface.</li></ul><p>Do not prepare account numbers, identity documents, tax-return files or other personal records for this form. A calculation can usually be reproduced with non-identifying sample amounts.</p>
  <h2>How a verified correction will be handled.</h2><ol><li>Check the report against the current source, assumptions and calculator version.</li><li>Reproduce the difference and determine whether it affects data, logic or presentation.</li><li>Correct the issue and add a targeted regression test where it helps prevent recurrence.</li><li>Record material changes in the affected page and the <a href="/updates/">updates log</a>, including the date and scope.</li></ol><p>This is the intended workflow. It does not claim that a report has already been received or resolved.</p>
  <h2>Published correction record.</h2><p>No calculation corrections have been recorded in this public log yet. Development and first-release notes are listed separately under <a href="/updates/">Updates</a>. A later material correction will be identified as a correction rather than silently presented as a routine refresh.</p>
</TrustPage>
